  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f$ be a differentiable function such that $2(x+2)^2 f(x)-3(x+2)^2=10 \\int_0^x(t+2) f(t) d t, x \\geq 0$. Then $f(2)$ is equal to ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "19",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$2(x+2)^2 f(x)-3(x+2)^2=10 \\int_0^x(t+2) f(t) d t$\nDifferentiating both side\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& 4(x+2) f(x)+2 f(x)(x+2)^2-6(x+2)=10(x+2) f(x) \\\\\n& =(x+2) \\frac{d y}{d x}-3 y=3 \\\\\n& \\frac{1}{3} \\int \\frac{d y}{y+1}=\\int \\frac{d x}{x+2} \\\\\n& \\ln |y+1=3 \\ln | x+2 \\mid+\\ln c \\\\\n& y+1=(x+2)^3 c \\\\\n& \\because y(0)=\\frac{3}{2} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{5}{16}=c \\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad y=\\frac{5}{16}(x+2)^3-1 \\\\\n& y(2)=\\frac{5}{16} \\times 64-1=19\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
